<BaseLayout title="Privacy & Advertising" description="Learn about kuoo.uk hosting, Google advertising, Cloudflare analytics, GitHub comments, affiliate links, and the privacy controls available from those services." lang="en">
  <article class="card">
    <h1>Privacy &amp; advertising</h1>
    <p>Updated: <time datetime="2026-10-29">29 October 2026</time>. This page describes the services used by AI Agent Hub at kuoo.uk.</p>
    <h2>Hosting and basic access data</h2>
    <p>The site is served through Cloudflare Pages. Serving and protecting a page involves connection information such as an IP address, the requested URL, browser information, and request timing. Cloudflare handles this information under its own service terms and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <h2>Google advertising</h2>
    <p>Pages include the Google AdSense script for publisher <code>pub-8837835283235973</code>. Google and its partners may use cookies or similar technologies to deliver, measure, and, where permitted, personalize advertising based on visits to this and other sites. Loading the script does not mean an advertisement is always available.</p>
    <p>Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">how Google uses information from partner sites</a>. You can review Google's advertising preferences in <a href="https://myadcenter.google.com/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">My Ad Center</a>. That external setting is not the same as giving or withdrawing site-specific consent.</p>
    <h2>Analytics and link interactions</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare Web Analytics, when enabled, measures page visits and performance. Site code also attempts to send selected navigation and outbound-link events, including the page path, language, link category, and label. These measurements are used to understand which guides and links are useful. The site does not ask you to register an account to read articles.</p>
    <h2>Comments, feedback, and external links</h2>
    <p>Article comments use Giscus and GitHub Discussions. Signing in and posting are handled by those services; posted comments and repository issues are public. See the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">GitHub Privacy Statement</a>. Do not post passwords, API keys, addresses, or other sensitive information.</p>
    <p>Some outbound links are affiliate links. Following one takes you to a third party that may use referral information or its own cookies. Its privacy terms apply there.</p>
    <h2>Your choices and questions</h2>
    <p>You can manage stored site data, cookies, and script permissions in your browser. Blocking a service may affect comments, analytics, or advertising. Where a consent message is shown, use its available controls. This privacy notice itself is not a consent request and does not replace any consent mechanism required in your region.</p>
    <p>For site questions or correction requests, see <a href="/en/contact/">Contact &amp; corrections</a>. Do not include private personal information in a public issue. For information held by Google, Cloudflare, or GitHub, use the privacy controls and request channels provided by that service.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
